gpu: report an indirect-buffer address outside the GPU window (0278)

The CP will fetch an indirect buffer from whatever address the two dwords in
the ring carry, and a bad one stalls submission instead of failing, which shows
up as "CP RPTR ... WPTR ... rem 0" plus client fence timeouts. raphael's GPU VA
window is [GVM_BASE, GVM_END) = [0x80000000, 0x100000000), so any IB address
outside it, or not page aligned, is a caller bug worth naming.

This only reports: each distinct bad address is printed once with its seqno and
the submission still goes ahead exactly as before, so the run behaves the same
while the log says which address is wrong.

Note for the next reader: SMMU CB1 FSR 0x400 with FAR 0x12de541f4ff28 is a
stale status bit from boot that sweet_gpu_submit() already clears; it is not a
runtime fault and must not be read as the cause of a stall.

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_a630.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_a630.c
@@ -3920,6 +3920,26 @@
 	if (!sweet_gpu_ready() || count == 0 || count > 128) {
 		return 0;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * 0278: the CP fetches an indirect buffer from whatever address the two dwords below carry, and
+	 * a bad one hangs submission instead of failing. raphael's GPU window is [GVM_BASE, GVM_END).
+	 * Report a distinct out-of-window or unaligned address once, and still submit: this only adds
+	 * diagnosis, it does not change behaviour.
+	 */
+	{
+		static uint64_t bad_ib_seen;
+		for (unsigned i = 0; i < count; i++) {
+			const uint64_t va = ib_iova[i];
+			if (va >= GVM_BASE && va < GVM_END && (va & 0xfff) == 0) {
+				continue;
+			}
+			if (__atomic_exchange_n(&bad_ib_seen, va, __ATOMIC_ACQ_REL) != va) {
+				printf("SWEET GPU: IB %u of %u at 0x%llx is outside the GPU window [0x%llx,0x%llx) or not page aligned (seqno %u)\n",
+				    i, count, (unsigned long long)va, (unsigned long long)GVM_BASE,
+				    (unsigned long long)GVM_END, a630_dev.seqno);
+			}
+		}
+	}
 	a630_last_active = mach_absolute_time();
 	if (!a630_awake && !gpu_resume()) {
 		return 0;
